  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 201 AM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nA well-defined pattern shift begins by Wednesday as changes in \nthe atmospheric circulation across the Pacific Ocean begins to \nimpact the monsoon plume over the southwest CONUS. An upper level \ntrough will deepen along the west coast and help to force the \nmonsoon high east into TX. 700-500mb layer flow will become more \nsoutherly over AZ and NM and allow rich monsoon moisture to surge\nnorth into the area. Models have been consistent and in good \nagreement that a convective disturbance will lift slowly north \ninto the monsoon plume from Wednesday thru Friday. Chances are \nincreasing for more widespread showers and storms over the area \nwith forecast PWATs supportive of heavy rainfall for parts of the \narea. This rich monsoon pattern may continue Saturday and Sunday \nwith an upper level trough persisting along the U.S. West Coast. \nForecast confidence is increasing but still guarded given the \noverall spotty nature of precip this summer and persistent heat.",
